SPEC-356a EG-1 -- EAGER REGISTRATION: ZERO BLANK CELLS ACROSS ALL COLUMNS,
                  FROM THE FIRST ROW
===========================================================================

WHAT THIS GATE ANSWERS. "Is a blank cell actually impossible now, or only
argued to be?" A reviewer can only take that on trust; a run settles it. The
gate has two limbs and BOTH are required.

WHY IT MATTERS. The derived POPULATION-ONLY column shape carries one named
delta over the shape it inherits: an `empty > 0` failing limb. Arming that limb
is only safe once a blank scrape-derived cell is unreachable on a correct
instrument, and a blank arises from exactly two causes -- (i) the series is not
yet registered when the scrape happens, and (ii) the scrape itself failed,
which returns nothing for every column alike. Limb (a) below proves (i) is
unrepresentable: all 33 pinned series render at 0 with ZERO observations taken.
Limb (b) proves the pair of fixes holds end-to-end over a real produced
artifact: zero empty fields across every column of every row, first row
included.

The parent lineage's committed evidence is what makes this non-theoretical: 10
of 10 whole-run `spec355-*.csv` files carry exactly one blank, in the
scrape-derived column, at `elapsed_secs = 0`. That is a BOOT PROPERTY, not
flakiness, and the `elapsed_secs == 0` tolerance is deliberately NOT adopted
here.

A NON-ZERO COUNT FAILS THIS GATE AND IS REPAIRED IN CODE OR IN THE SAMPLER.
Relaxing a column check is not an available repair.

================================================================================
LIMB (a) -- DETERMINISTIC, IN-PROCESS: the first render with NO observations
================================================================================

With the Prometheus recorder installed first, the observer is constructed, NO
observations are taken, and the render is taken through `PrometheusHandle::
render()`. The assertion is that all 33 pinned names are present -- the 15
counters at 0, the 11 gauges at 0, and each of the 7 histograms rendering BOTH
`<name>_sum` and `<name>_count`. `describe_*` does NOT register in this
exporter and is never the registration mechanism; the eager touch at recorder
construction is.

INVOCATION (verbatim, as run):

  SDKROOT=$(/usr/bin/xcrun --sdk macosx --show-sdk-path) \
  cargo test --release -p topgun-server --lib -- \
    tombstone_frontier_impl::tests::every_pinned_prune_series_is_present_in_the_first_render \
    --exact --nocapture

